{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/441872-ever-run-a-crossover-non-directly-to-other-wod-lines","id":441872,"title":"Ever run a Crossover (Non Directly to other WoD Lines?)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-14T15:11:42-07:00","id":441872,"title":"Ever run a Crossover (Non Directly to other WoD Lines?)","content":"things like Dungeons and Dragons or Call of Cthulhu, or even involving a novel or comic or tv show or movie xD!<br /> <br /> i used to play a campaing of Werewolf The Wild West but within the Deadlands Setting (making the Reckoners a manifestation of The Wyrm), was fun. good times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T16:14:40-07:00","id":441934,"title":"","content":"Not with WoD, but I did run a crossover between AD&amp;D2e, TORG and Gamma World that was rather amusing. I had originally planned to crossover with Star Trek as well, but decided that was too much, lol! If Mage had existed back then, I'd have thrown that in there too, no doubt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T16:26:50-07:00","id":441949,"title":"","content":"I'm not exactly sure what you are asking here, but yes.<br /> <br /> For the WoD, I've run both crossovers that allowed all of the lines, such as Vampires, Werewolves, Wraiths, etc, and I've also run a few things like WoD Silent Hill, and it was freakin' amazing.<br /> <br /> I've had a few Marvel Characters show up in WoD games as well. In one instance I can recall of the top of my head, I had Dare Devil show up as a way to really screw with one character that was using Auspex in an attempt to study the city's population, having fun as I was trying to describe what the player was seeing through his &lt;sonar&gt; vision.<br /> <br /> I've also done a few games that stole a lot from nWoD's Night Horrors series, and included a lot of odd and unique &quot;things&quot;, which can range from a Mage that honestly believed he was a Jedi, to Cthulhuian beings, to the X-Men.<br /> <br /> I almost, but never actually got to, play a Celestial Chorus mage that believed he was a 3rd Edition D&amp;D Cleric, trapped in a strange world. (Sort of the opposite of the D&amp;D cartoon).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T09:59:47-07:00","id":442713,"title":"","content":"Not crossover, but I had Virtual Adept sorcerer from 23 century's technocratic semy-utopia.<br /> <br /> But my first Vampire game has lot of metaplot crossover with &quot;Hellraiser&quot;. At least, in campaign's mythology...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T10:56:21-07:00","id":442823,"title":"","content":"always wanted to do a WoD discworld crossover, but never knew how to handle Death.<br /> <br /> And whenever i send a HITmark in mage, i go all terminator with it<br /> <br /> also...i need to do a Firefly crossover someday...Some Day..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T14:35:08-07:00","id":443121,"title":"","content":"Like I've said before I helped set up and played in a DAW crossover with A Song of Ice and Fire. It was fairly enjoyable but now having a chance to pick up the ASoIF RPG Rulebook and seeing its rather in-depth House creation I would love to do something with that in DAV, DAM or DAI.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T06:24:57-07:00","id":447617,"title":"","content":"I've used the storyteller system for a lot of things, usually with some moderate alterations.<br /> <br /> The most successful effort was quite a long time ago, and it was sort of a Dragonlance style home-made world a couple buddies and I worked on over the course of a few years. I used the basic Mage system, sort of combining Quintessence and Paradox as Mana so that the same system worked but Paradox resulted in forced mana costs, potentially damaging the mage if he didn't have the buffer to pay that unexpected cost.<br /> <br /> It worked pretty well, but the goal was really to provide that dynamic magic system to a more classic D&amp;D type game.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've been sort of working on another adaptation of the ST system, trying to simplify it for kids. Not sure what kind of world I will use with this eventually, something like a D&amp;D world (Hero Kids type stuff) or maybe a Harry Potter thing (kids love the Potter).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T09:11:26-07:00","id":447759,"title":"","content":"Sailor Moon is part of my WoD head-canon.<br /> <br /> Also, I've planned for games set in cities from the Grand Theft Auto series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T20:23:51-07:00","id":448743,"title":"","content":"I personally like the WoD system for its ability to write up human character concepts better than most other systems.<br /> I've used it to put together an Arkham Horror (Call of Cthulhu board game) chronicle. All of the characters were written up (including from most of the expansions) for the players to choose from to play. Each had some special merit that was just for them.<br /> Aside from that, I've included a lot of the Soul Calibur characters in my Renaissance timelines. The Big Bad for one game was a Spiral Ahroun wielding Nightmare. Was kind of fun.<br /> Let's see.....I've used Highlander Immortals (there was a fan-made supplement for them) in more than a couple of WoD games, though they've mostly been NPCs.<br /> There was a high fantasy Dark Ages game that game included a mixed group of supernaturals that were hunting the last of the dragons (with varying success). That played a lot more like D&amp;D than a traditional DA game.<br /> I have the crossover book for Werewolf the Wild West and Deadlands, but haven't had the chance to run a game using it as of yet.<br /> <br /> My wife wrote up an outline to use the WoD system to run a game set in Stephen King's interconnected universe.<br /> <br /> Those are off the top of my head, but I think I've got notes at home for a few more games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:55:40-07:00","id":455970,"title":"","content":"I several times blended Mages with Novas, I tried to ballance the two types by giving Mages a larger dice pool for Magic. My gaming groups kept falling apart because of the players changing lives. So I never really found out if my crossover worked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T13:49:50-07:00","id":462646,"title":"","content":"Mages in games I've run or played in have crossed over (through Umbral travel, essentially) with (excluding the echoes of our own world's past histories): Aliens (as in xenomorphs), Star Trek, zombie apocalypses, 1984, Gattaca, BSG, and probably quite a few more I'm forgetting.<br /> <br /> A Hermetic throwing a fireball at a xenomorph or a Euthantos correcting the Wheel in a zombie universe are fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T02:56:27-07:00","id":465851,"title":"","content":"I've ran Guilty Gear mixed with Aberrant as well as Cthulhu styled elements in WoD, though WoD has it's own Cthulhuesque creatures for these themes as well, Chulorviah, Fomori and the Neverborn to name a few.<br /> <br /> I've also ran, originally as a convention game, a Half Life/Mage thing with it happening in a Technocratic research facility and the players were a team of Technocrats making an evaluation tour through it when all hell broke loose.<br /> <br /> I'am about to run, when I get time for it, a Fomori game inspired by Resident Evil series, particularly the Operation Raccoon City game. Though it is not really a crossover as much as taking inspiration from it and applying it to Pentex/Fomori instead of Umbrella/Infected.<br /> <br /> One of My Sorcerer's Crusade games featured Soul Edge from Soul Calibur series though the players were too scared of it to touch it and left it be ultimately. That same game also crossovered slightly with Exalted: the Fair Folk a bit earlier.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there have been plenty of other over the years but these are the ones currently popping to mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T06:53:56-07:00","id":469304,"title":"","content":"I went with the cross-over route (both in terms of mixed narratives, as well as shifting game mechanics) between Ravenloft and CWoD (starting with Vampire) back in '91. I'll start running a Dark Ages mixed-splat in two weeks that has aspects of Ravenloft in it, set in the 1150's. Makes perfect sense, across the board.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]}